From 0820511d18c9c978042f72547196c5c4797968f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tunkoal <tunkoal@163.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:35:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Settings: allow twilight schedule to start without a
 cached fix

On Rothko 1795050579 after recovery data wipe, API-first Settings displays the pending-location dialog but rejects auto mode when the fused cache is empty. UiModeManager therefore cannot register TwilightService to obtain location. A direct framework mode selection from the same state did register location requests; subsequent Metok location delivered a TwilightState and sunset alarm.

Match the existing legacy controller by persisting the choice when location is enabled, retaining pending and disabled feedback. The provider overlay controls routing and cannot initialize the fused cache before the user selects a schedule. This fixes the Settings path for any device that uses it without modifying providers, timers, or other theme modes.

Exercise the empty-cache path in the existing preference and storage Robotests. Both changed Kotlin production files compile against the previous build jars and git diff --check passed. Full Robotests, image build, and clean-data UI acceptance remain pending.

